<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
	xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
	<modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
	<parent>
		<groupId>com.stucray</groupId>
		<artifactId>raptor-parent</artifactId>
		<version>0.1.1-SNAPSHOT</version>
		<relativePath>../pom.xml</relativePath>
	</parent>
	<artifactId>raptor-schema</artifactId>
	<description>The raw, query and batch Flyway migrations, and nothing else. Published.</description>

	<!--
		A jar of SQL, deliberately with no code and no dependencies (#246).

		The migrations lived in `acquisition` until analysis moved out of paddock
		(PRD #245). `query` is now a published contract, and a consumer's tests
		need the real shape of it: the schema is built from these files, not from
		a second description of them. Publishing `acquisition` itself would hand
		the consumer the recorder, the ingest and the projection jobs to get at a
		directory of SQL, so the directory became its own artifact instead.

		`acquisition` depends on this module and still loads the files from
		`classpath:db/acquisition`, so moving them changed no behaviour.

		ONE LOCATION. `db/acquisition` is the raw/query/batch line, and it is
		paddock's own: AcquisitionMigrations applies exactly this directory to the
		live database.

		There was a second, `db/contract`, carrying a copy of `team_alias`'s DDL
		for consumers (#263). It went in #315, when overround-analysis took the
		table over as `analysis.team_alias`, mastered and migrated in its own
		repository. Releases up to and including the one that shipped it still
		contain the file.

		For consumers: apply `db/acquisition` to a TEST database only, with the
		same settings AcquisitionMigrations uses: schemas raw, query, batch;
		default schema query; history table flyway_schema_history_acquisition;
		createSchemas; and the `readerPassword` and `analysisPassword`
		placeholders, which V6 and V27 need to give paddock_reader and
		overround_analysis their logins.

		paddock's own database is migrated by paddock and nobody else.
	-->
</project>
